/-!
# The alternating group `A₅` is a D-group

Bender's definition of a D-group (`GorensteinWalter.IsDGroup`) has no direct
`A₅` clause, so this file proves `IsDGroup (alternatingGroup (Fin 5))` through
the exceptional isomorphism `A₅ ≅ PSL₂(ZMod 5)`:

* `alternatingGroupFive_equiv_PSL2` exhibits the isomorphism.  The sixty
  elements of `A₅` are paired with sixty representatives in `SL₂(ZMod 5)`
  (`sigmaᵢ` / `repMatᵢ`, generated by a script); the class map is a
  homomorphism and injective.  Rather than checking all `60²` pairs, the
  homomorphism property is verified on the two generators
  `a5x = (0 1)(2 3)` and `a5y = (0 2 4)` (and their inverses) by `decide`,
  and extended to all of `A₅` via `Subgroup.closure_induction_left` using
  `closure_a5x_a5y`.  Bijectivity then follows from the equality of the two
  cardinalities `60`.

* `pPrimeCore_two_alternatingGroupFive` shows the `2'`-core of `A₅` is trivial
  (using simplicity of `A₅`), so `A₅ ⧸ pPrimeCore 2 A₅ ≃* A₅`.

* `hasCyclicOrDihedralSylowTwo_alternatingGroupFive` shows the Sylow
  `2`-subgroups of `A₅` are Klein four groups, i.e. `DihedralGroup 2`.

The linear clause of `IsDGroup` is then instantiated with `K = ZMod 5`
(`IsOddPrimePower 5`) and `L = ⊤`.
-/

noncomputable section

open scoped MatrixGroups
open scoped Matrix
open Equiv.Perm

namespace CFSG.GorensteinWalter

universe u

set_option maxRecDepth 100000
set_option maxHeartbeats 8000000

private abbrev A5SL2 := Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup (Fin 2) (ZMod 5)

/-! ## The isomorphism `A₅ ≅ PSL₂(ZMod 5)` -/

/-- Decidable equality for permutations of `Fin 5`, needed to evaluate the
lookup table `repPerm` by computation. -/
instance : DecidableEq (Equiv.Perm (Fin 5)) := fun a b =>
  decidable_of_iff (∀ i : Fin 5, a i = b i) ⟨Equiv.ext, fun h i => congrArg (fun e => e i) h⟩

/-- Decidable membership in `alternatingGroup (Fin 5)`, needed for the
computational verifications below. -/
instance : DecidablePred (fun σ : Equiv.Perm (Fin 5) => σ ∈ alternatingGroup (Fin 5)) :=
  sign.decidableMemKer

